ved  with any of the individuals in months  and so okay if you haven't been around  these people you didn't do it but then  as it unfolded throughout the day it  appears that the argument will be if it  ever gets to this point that he arranged  for someone else to do it that's the  message that screams out from between  the lines of the statement that was  issued yesterday by the victim's lawyer  all right the purchase  for the Carolina Panthers is now  finalized but I guess they for 2.2 or  2.3 billion they also threw in jerry  richardson statue okay did the did the  new ownership want to take down the  stunt like was there a statute of  limitations here mike well you know the  owner said yesterday he's contractually  obligated to keep the statue which is  hardly a ringing endorsement when it  comes to the design well you know i have  to keep you know i have to keep it up  now it's possible there's some issue  with the city owning the land where the  statue is and maybe David Tepper  providing some cover for the city so  they don't start getting a bunch of  tough questions about why they'd allow  this statue to continue to stand but the  statue is going to continue to stand and  I'd hate to think that jerry richardson  could have gotten even more money for  the team but he gave up some of it so he  could secure the you know ongoing  placement of the statue well into the  future outside of the stadium why I  didn't even know there was a statue of  Jerry Richardson are there any other  statues of any other owners in the NFL I  don't think there are but you know what  this is probably given them all some  pretty good ideas well Jerry Jones Jerry  Jones suit statue of a guy in a suit  holding a football it's the strangest  thing nothing inspires you quite like  that you know when you show up at  Lambeau and you see Lombardi you know  Chicago Stadium with Jordan and then you  show up with the Carolina Panthers and  Jerry Richardson's there in a suit nice  yeah I agree with you Jerry Jones  probably probably already has the the  plans in place and it will be bigger and  nicer and more impressive than the Jerry  Richardson statue the NFL Players  Association had a statement yesterday  you know talking about the NFL's new  anthem policy why why did they wait so  long to put this statement out well  here's what they did they filed a  grievance and they waited until the  basically last minute they could file a  grievance under the collective  bargaining agreement cuz I think they've  been trying to work with the NFL behind  the scenes because this  not going to be a popular move right  anybody who is taking up the cause that  ultimately supports players not standing  for the anthem puts themselves in in the  the target zone for all of the criticism  whether it's from the president or  anyone else out there who insists that  the players should be standing so I  think the NFLPA was hoping to work it  out before they had to follow the  grievance now they've filed the  grievance and they plan to talk to the  NFL and that's what should have happened  back in August in 2016 I put a lot of  this on the NFL Dan they should have the  moment Colin Kaepernick was was seen  sitting during the national anthem in a  preseason game and the NFL told me I  said well hey what's your take on this  he said players are encouraged to stand  but not required this all comes from a  flawed policy the NFL wrote nine years  ago they should have engaged with the  Union to then to come up with a policy  that requires the players to stand they  didn't because I think they didn't want  to make a concession because if you ask  the Union hey we want something the  Union says we want something back that's  how it works  now that they've waited two years it's  gonna take a lot more I think to get the  the players to get in on that point than  it would have back in August of 2016  what would you suggest well if you were  mediating like advising the NFL how  would you handle this flag controversy  well I'd say hey NFL you have to engage  with the Union sit down at the  bargaining table and you want all the  players to agree to stand at attention  and respect the flag during the anthem  and you have to listen to what the Union  would want in return and I don't know at  this point what the Union would want in  return a lot of times people say well  get rid of the marijuana policy with the  Marijuana Policy it's a non-issue  because if you're smart you know how to  avoid a positive test I don't know that  the NFLPA is banging the drum to get rid  of that but maybe there's something the  NFLPA is looking for that you know it's  fairly significant and it's important to  them and this anthem policy is important  to the NFL and they could come up with  some sort of a quid pro quo a  give-and-take a back-and-forth to solve  this but I think the NFL's stubbornness  contributed to the problem in 2016 they  didn't want to give anything up to get a  commitment to stand and now that it's  going to cost even more to make it  happen they don't want to do it either I  just want  Ram it through the way that they choose  and and and if they have to fight they  have to fight but they could lose  because the arguments very simple dan  once this right exists the players have  the right to protest the nfo gave them  that right you can't just take it away  without sitting down and talking to the  Union that's the argument and it seems  pretty common sensical and if the Union  wins that then the policy gets rolled  back to what it was before May and the  NFL still has a major problem going into  the 2018 season thank you Mike as always  we appreciate your time all right Dan  Mike Florio pro football talk live on  NBCSN NBC radio as well for more Dan  Patrick show to the audience channel 239  on DirecTV or download the Dan Patrick  show at  [Music]
 

